E('gilgamesh king|uruk', 'Uruk was one of the first true cities in the world.', 'It flourished in southern Mesopotamia from about 4000 BC.', 'It may have had 40,000 to 80,000 people at its height.', 'Some of the earliest writing has been found there.', 'Its legendary king was Gilgamesh.', 'The name Iraq may derive from Uruk.')
E('ur|royal tombs of ur', 'Ur was an important Sumerian city in southern Mesopotamia.', 'It flourished in the 3rd millennium BC.', 'Its great ziggurat was built around 2100 BC.', 'Leonard Woolley excavated its royal tombs in the 1920s.', 'They held treasures like the Standard of Ur and a golden lyre.')
E('catal huyuk|çatalhöyük|catalhoyuk', 'Çatalhöyük was one of the world’s earliest large farming towns.', 'It was occupied from about 7100 to 5700 BC, in modern Turkey.', 'Houses were packed together with no streets.', 'People entered through holes in the roofs.', 'Walls were decorated with paintings of animals.')
E('jericho', 'Jericho is one of the oldest continuously inhabited cities in the world.', 'People have lived there for over 10,000 years.', 'It had a stone wall and tower by about 8000 BC.', 'It lies in the West Bank.', 'The biblical story says its walls fell to trumpets.')
E('gobekli tepe', 'Göbekli Tepe is an ancient stone monument in south-east Turkey.', 'It was built around 9500 BC, thousands of years before Stonehenge.', 'It has huge carved T-shaped pillars.', 'It was built by hunter-gatherers, surprising archaeologists.', 'It may be one of the world’s oldest temples.')
E('terracotta warriors', 'The Terracotta Warriors are life-sized clay soldiers buried with China’s first emperor.', 'They were made around 210 BC.', 'Each figure has a different face.', 'They were originally brightly painted.', 'Farmers found them in 1974 near Xi’an.')
E('dunhuang|mogao caves', 'The Mogao Caves near Dunhuang are a complex of Buddhist cave temples in China.', 'They were carved from the 4th to the 14th century.', 'They lie on the Silk Road.', 'A sealed library cave found in 1900 held tens of thousands of documents.', 'It included the Diamond Sutra, the oldest dated printed book, from 868.')
E('diamond sutra', 'The Diamond Sutra is a Buddhist text and the oldest known dated printed book.', 'This copy was printed in 868.', 'It was found in the Mogao Caves.', 'It is a scroll about five metres long.', 'It is kept in the British Library.')
E('codex|codices|illuminated manuscripts', 'Illuminated manuscripts are handwritten books decorated with gold, silver and colour.', 'They were made mostly in medieval Europe, from about 500 to 1500.', 'Monks often made them.', 'The Book of Kells, from around 800, is a famous example.', 'Printing made them rare.')
E('book of kells', 'The Book of Kells is a richly decorated manuscript of the Gospels.', 'It was made around AD 800.', 'It was probably created by monks on the island of Iona.', 'It is kept at Trinity College Dublin.', 'Its intricate decoration is world-famous.')
